### What changed compared to a “load‑all‑at‑once” approach?

| Before (load all)                               | After (streaming)                              |
|-------------------------------------------------|-----------------------------------------------|
| `fs.readFileSync` → entire file in memory       | `fs.createReadStream` → reads chunks lazily   |
| `csvParse(csvString, options, callback)`       | `csvParse(options)` → returns a stream object |
| You get an array of all rows at once            | You get one row at a time via the `readable` event |
| Memory usage grows with file size               | Memory stays roughly constant regardless of file size |

